# KHI Dashboard

## Project
Kurdish Heritage Institute (KHI) CMS Admin Dashboard.
Private panel (no SEO). Single admin role. Deployed on Vercel.

## Package Manager
Always use pnpm. Never suggest npm or yarn.

## Stack
- Next.js 14+ App Router, TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui + ReUI
- Heroicons (NOT Lucide)
- next/image for all images
- TanStack Query + Axios for data fetching
- Zustand for client/UI state
- React Hook Form + Zod for forms
- Tiptap for rich text editing
- next-intl for UI strings (single fixed locale, no routing)
- Recharts via shadcn ChartContainer
- shadcn DataTable (TanStack Table)

## Component Usage — CRITICAL
- Always use shadcn/ui and ReUI components first.
  Before writing any custom UI, check if shadcn or ReUI already
  has the component (Button, Input, Dialog, Sheet, Table,
  Card, Badge, Tabs, Select, Checkbox, etc.).
- Never replace or rewrite an existing shadcn/ReUI component
  with a custom implementation. Extend via className/variants only.
- Never overwrite existing component files in components/ui/.
  These are owned by shadcn/ReUI — treat them as read-only.
- Follow existing patterns and examples already in the codebase.
  If a pattern exists for forms, tables, dialogs — replicate it,
  do not invent a new one.
- Custom components go in components/modules/ or components/shared/,
  never in components/ui/.
- Use shadcn variants (variant=, size=) before reaching for
  custom Tailwind classes.
- When in doubt: less custom code, more shadcn/ReUI composition.

## Auth
Spring Boot backend owns JWT + Google OAuth.
Frontend: Axios interceptors attach JWT, Zustand holds session.

## i18n & RTL
- UI is Kurdish Sorani (ckb) only — always RTL, no language switcher
- dir="rtl" applied globally at <html> level, never toggled
- next-intl config uses a single fixed locale (ckb), no [locale] URL segment
- UI strings live in messages/ckb.json only
- Content fields are bilingual: Sorani (ckb) + Kurmanji (kmr)
- Name bilingual fields: title_ckb / title_kmr, body_ckb / body_kmr, etc.
- Content forms always render both dialect fields (e.g. tabs: Sorani | Kurmanji)
- Apply dir="rtl" for ckb fields, dir="ltr" for kmr fields when rendering

## Folder Structure
app/(auth)/login
app/(dashboard)/overview
app/(dashboard)/projects
app/(dashboard)/news
app/(dashboard)/image-collection
app/(dashboard)/soundtracks
app/(dashboard)/videos
app/(dashboard)/writings
app/(dashboard)/about
app/(dashboard)/contact
app/(dashboard)/service
components/ui         → shadcn/ReUI primitives — READ ONLY, never modify
components/layout     → Sidebar, Topbar, Shell, ThemeToggle
components/modules    → Per-section components
components/shared     → Toast, ErrorBoundary, MediaUploader, RichEditor
lib/api               → Axios instance + interceptors
lib/store             → Zustand stores
lib/validators        → Zod schemas
lib/hooks             → Custom hooks
messages/ckb.json     → UI strings (Sorani only)
types/                → Global TS types & API response shapes

## Conventions
- All components: TypeScript, named exports
- Errors: inline on form fields + global toasts (no redundant components)
- Pagination: page + size (offset-based)
- Media uploads: multipart/form-data to Spring Boot backend
- Environments: .env.local (dev) / .env.production

## Design
- Fonts: Geist Sans + Geist Mono, antialiased
- Radius: ~0.5rem
- Theme: Light + Dark toggle (D key), system default
- Light: white bg, warm dark text, teal primary, mint primary-fg,
         warm light gray muted/borders, strong red destructive
- Dark: warm charcoal bg, off-white text, deeper teal primary,
        card slightly lighter than bg, semi-transparent white borders,
        lighter red destructive
- Charts: blue family (--chart-1 to --chart-5) both modes
- Sidebar matches theme

## Typography
Three fonts are configured — use each strictly by role:

- Noto Naskh Arabic  → Titles & headings (h1, h2, h3, card titles, page headings)
- Vazirmatn          → UI text (nav, sidebar, buttons, labels, badges, stats, numbers)
- Noto Sans Arabic   → Body & subtext (descriptions, subtitles, tooltips, table cells)
- Geist Mono         → Code blocks only

Font assignment by element:
- Page title          : Noto Naskh Arabic, weight 600
- Section heading     : Noto Naskh Arabic, weight 500
- Card title          : Noto Naskh Arabic, weight 500
- Nav / sidebar items : Vazirmatn, weight 400
- Buttons             : Vazirmatn, weight 500
- Form labels         : Vazirmatn, weight 400
- Badges / tags       : Vazirmatn, weight 500
- Stat numbers        : Vazirmatn, weight 600
- Body / description  : Noto Sans Arabic, weight 400
- Subtext / muted     : Noto Sans Arabic, weight 400
- Tooltips            : Noto Sans Arabic, weight 400

Never use a font outside its assigned role.
Never use Geist Sans or system fonts for Arabic/Kurdish text.
Always set font-feature-settings and text rendering for Arabic scripts.